Z||000008||maryjane||11-24-2001||12:52 PM||||My 1st wife w/ new baby: Sweetheart, we can sell your Vette, and keep my Mustang (6cyl)<BR>because we don't need two cars but we need something with a backseat. That's the day she jumped the shark. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jake_Dragon||11-24-2001||01:23 PM||||It will never make it home, it will burn up before you can fix it, its too loud, and you dont need two of them.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/left.gif">                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">                       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/right.gif">           <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt2_3.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroKyle||11-24-2001||01:41 PM||||Crash's motto.<P>"If the car can take it, do it."<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokylesig_1.gif">      <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||watts||11-24-2001||01:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by avengador1:<BR><B>Fill the manual transmission with A/T fluid...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well...  in defense of somebody somewhere...  SOME manual trannies DO use ATF.  My '86 S-10 4*4 uses Dexron II in the tranny (T5) and transfer case (says so right in the factory owners handbook) as an example.<P>But as for bad advise - when I was about 19 I had a Porsche 914.  Buddies dad was a 'pro' (from Greece) mechanic so i usually listened to him.  Anyhow, at one point my lil' car was making one hell of a racket - he listened to it and said that the rod bearings were on the way out and that I should rebuild the whole engine ASAP.<P>Turns out that on closer inspection when I had the time...  A leaking exhaust O-ring (they don't use normal gaskets) sounds a lot like a knocking rod bearing to some people.  Few minutes and a $2 o-ring later it purred like a kitten again.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jaei Sun||11-24-2001||05:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Stupid Car advice given to you<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Buy a Chrysler" -lea Iccocca||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fformula88||11-24-2001||09:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by watts:<BR><B> Well...  in defense of somebody somewhere...  SOME manual trannies DO use ATF.  My '86 S-10 4*4 uses Dexron II in the tranny (T5) and transfer case (says so right in the factory owners handbook) as an example.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok, let me clarify my statement since it seems to have managed to upset the masses here.  Besides this post, I also received an anonymous email about it.<P>The advise was not specifically for a manual transmission that specified Dexron (or other ATF fluid) in its manual.  It was for a car that specified regular oil.  You should always use what is specified in the manual, and should not use anything else.<P>In the context of the post, someone recommended filling a transmission that called for gear oil with ATF fluid for smoother operation.  This is a very bad idea.  The chemical composition of the ATF fluid will eat away at the rubber parts inside this type of transmission.  Another respondant to the thread admitting to destroying his tranny this way.<P>Sorry for the confusion.  Basically, if you want to put a fluid into your car, pick up your owners manual and find out what it calls for!  <P>(BTW, knowing who is emailing you can be nice too.  If you wanna float me an email, great!  Just clue me in to whom I am responding to.  Thanks!)||||reg||1
Z||000014||Pheagey||11-24-2001||10:05 PM||||   "...I'd tel them to take that Fiero and stick it where to sun don't shire! alone with there $160 tow bill." I received this shortly after I was infor5mted th eHioghway Patrol had my car towed ('cause someon stole the tires).<BR>   Needless to say I still have it, and a nice set or rims on some rubber that'll last me a lil' while..<BR>   <P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed;<BR>Have you seen my website yet?<BR>Http://www.LithiumEffects/pheageysfeiro<BR>"The car formaly know as, and has now reverted back to being known as, Pheagey's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000015||Gary W||11-24-2001||11:19 PM||||Had a '76 or so CJ-7 which needed a heater core. It was the middle of winter, and I didn't have time or space to do it, so I took it to a garage near work. Told the guy it needed a heater core. He calls a couple of hours later and says "You need a motor."<BR>Huh?? "Yep, that's why you have no heat." Told him not to do anything. He already had the whole friggin' engine halfway out. Tried to charge $300 for his "trouble". Jerk.<P>Another time, I blew a tire on the infamous Garden State Parkway - no spare, of course. Tow company tried to charge over $300 for a 10 mile tow and a tire. While I was waiting/arguing, I watched the secretary call 5 people in a row and tell them all that their stalled cars needed $500 computers.||||reg||1
